/-
# Coprime action of a four-group on an odd-order group

This file proves the coprime-action generation theorem used as Peterfalvi I Ch. I §1 (9)
(= Gorenstein, *Finite Groups*, Theorem 5.3.16): a finite group of **odd** order on which a
four-group `{1,a,b,ab}` acts by automorphisms is generated by the centralisers of the three
involutions `a`, `b`, `ab`.

The proof is by strong induction on `|G|`:

* if `G` is abelian we use `Work.ThreePoints.abelian_elemCent_sup_eq_top` (elementary: the
  `C₂ × C₂`-eigenspace decomposition, using that `2` is invertible on an odd-order abelian
  group);
* if the centre `Z(G)` is a proper non-trivial subgroup we reduce to `Z(G)` (abelian) and to
  `G ⧸ Z(G)` (smaller), using the quotient lemma `Work.ThreePoints.elemCent_map_mk`;
* if `Z(G) = ⊥` then `G` is not a `p`-group, and for each prime `p ∣ |G|` an invariant Sylow
  `p`-subgroup `P` is a proper subgroup, so `P` is contained in the join by induction; the
  prime powers `|P|` then multiply to `|G|`, whence `|G|` divides the order of the join.

Centralisers of single elements of the acting group are `Work.ThreePoints.elemCent`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.ThreePoints.FourGroupCoprimeDefs
import Submission.Work.Coprime.Internal
import Submission.Work.Coprime.Normalizer
import Submission.Work.Coprime.exists_invariant_sylow
import Submission.Work.ThreePoints.abelian_elemCent_sup_eq_top
import Submission.Work.ThreePoints.elemCent_map_mk
import Submission.Work.ThreePoints.card_dvd_of_prime_pow_factorization_dvd

